## 7. Acceptance checklist

### Evidence and review

- [ ] Target artifact identity/SHA is recorded.
- [ ] Required target roots and relations have reopenable evidence.
- [ ] Required `UNRESOLVED` items are blocked or explicitly deferred off-path.
- [ ] Raw diff stays inside allowed writes.
- [ ] Producer and accepting reviewer are different model families.
- [ ] Cross-model reviewer verdict is recorded against raw evidence and raw diff.

### Build provenance

- [ ] Baseline/overlay manifest passes before review and build.
- [ ] Build-input manifest covers source, scripts, archives/DSOs and linker/provider order relevant to this feature.
- [ ] Fresh native-x86 build has compile fail=0, link exit=0 and undefined refs=0.
- [ ] Candidate binary SHA/Build ID and active process executable SHA match.

### Static checks

- [ ] <layout / enum / call closure / table-reader / binding-shape check>
- [ ] <coverage-diff: ported/folded/deferred/forgotten=0 for scoped closure>

